This project builds on prior work it does not own:

- FR-Spec: Frequency-Ranked Speculative Sampling (Zhao et al., ACL 2025) — the idea of restricting a drafter's output
  projection to a frequency-ranked vocabulary subset while the target verifies over the full vocabulary.
  https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.198.pdf
- MiaAI-Lab's DGX Spark kits for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next — the vLLM MTP draft-vocabulary overlay (`MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB`),
  the 47k en+code floor, the byte-fallback pinning and the language-extension method this repository follows.
  https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Single-DGX-Spark
- Korean Wikipedia — the frequency source for the Korean vocabularies. Text © Wikipedia contributors,
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The vocabulary files contain token ids ranked by
  frequency, not Wikipedia text; the attribution is carried in every file header regardless.

No customer or private corpus is used in any published file.
